Given text: {There’s certainly a widespread cultural belief in the value of greater willpower and self-discipline, as a glance at any self-help shelf or magazine rack will attest.}
Discussion that supports the given lines: {Findings show that people with greater self-control experience benefits such as higher productivity and success at school and work, greater success and satisfaction in their relationships, and they are viewed as more trustworthy by their peers. Naturally, these impressive outcomes shine a highly favourable light on the trait, and they jibe with the way that willpower is vaunted in popular culture.}
The author explicitly mentions the attributes presented in Options A, C and D - thus, these options are consistent with the discussion in the passage. Contrarily, the relationship between self-control and socially damaging activities has not been discussed in the passage - furthermore, the author does not use this to explain why greater willpower is viewed favourably in society. 
Hence, Option B is the correct choice.
